    "key_shape": "{'static': {literal: {kind: count}}, 'dynamic_sites': int}",
    "why": "DF-15. The Section 8.4 no-loss gate counts a citation only if its literal resolves onto an article in that edition articles_8_4.json, and the generator raises on non-8.4 content in those caches, so Part 4/5/6 citations are dropped at scan time and could be deleted without failing anything. Measured 2026-09-18: 213 sites inside the 8.4 gate, 173 outside it. This baseline guards the outside. It does NOT widen the coverage attestation, which is a Section 8.4 document and stays one.",
    "two_populations": "static: a plain string literal, keyed exactly by {literal: {kind: count}} with no file path in the key so a rename cannot invalidate it. dynamic_sites: one integer for an article= whose value is a variable or an f-string the scanner cannot fold to a name. Those cannot be keyed honestly (the scanner renders such an f-string as a fragment, an extraction artefact that appears in no audit) but they can be counted, so deleting one drops the total."
